.TH QORE 1 "2026 May 14" "Qore 2.3" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qore \- interpreter for the Qore programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qore
[\fIoption\fP]...
[\fIprogram\-file\fP]
[\fIprogram\-args\fP]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBQore\fR is a modular, multi-threaded scripting language with optional strong
typing, procedural and object-oriented features, built-in SQL integration,
HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 support, and a clean syntax designed for readability.
This release includes the IR execution engine, LLVM JIT compilation, tiered
execution, and AOT compilation support for scripts and user modules.
.PP
When invoked without a program file and standard input is a terminal,
\fBqore\fR starts an interactive REPL (read-eval-print loop).
When a program file is given, it is parsed and executed.
The \fB\-e\fR option allows executing code supplied on the command line.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "General Options"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version, build, and library information, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-short\-version
Show only the version number and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version\-animation
Show an animated 3D version logo and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-charset =\fIencoding\fP
Set the default character set encoding for the program.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-define =\fIkey\fP[=\fIvalue\fP]
Set a parse define.
Multiple \fB\-D\fP flags may be given.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exec =\fIcode\fP
Execute the Qore program given as a string on the command line.
.TP
.B \-\-exec\-mode =\fImode\fP
Select the execution engine.
\fImode\fP may be \fBast\fP, \fBir\fP, \fBjit\fP, or \fBtiered\fP.
\fBtiered\fP is the default and promotes hot functions from AST execution to
IR and then to JIT-compiled native code.
.TP
.B \-\-ir\-dump
Dump the IR representation before execution.
.TP
.B \-\-ir\-fallback\-warn
Print a warning on standard error when IR execution falls back to AST.
.TP
.B \-\-ir\-fallback\-report
Print IR fallback counts by category when the process exits.
.TP
.B \-\-jit\-ir\-threshold =\fIN\fP
In tiered mode, set the number of calls before a function is promoted to IR.
The default is 100.
.TP
.B \-\-jit\-jit\-threshold =\fIN\fP
In tiered mode, set the number of calls before a function is promoted to JIT.
The default is 1000.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-load =\fImodule\fP
Load the named module immediately at startup.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-show\-module\-errors
Display errors encountered while loading and initializing modules.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-set\-parse\-option =\fIoption\fP
Set a parse option (e.g., \fB\-penable\-debug\fP, \fB\-pno\-database\fP).
Use \fB\-H\fP to list available parse options.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exec\-class [=\fIclassname\fP]
Instantiate a class with the same name as the file (or \fIclassname\fP
if given).
Implies \fB\-\-no\-top\-level\fP.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-eval =\fIexpression\fP
Evaluate a Qore expression and display the result.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-time\-zone =\fIzone\fP
Set the time zone.
\fIzone\fP is either a region name (e.g., \fBEurope/Prague\fP)
or a UTC offset like \fB+02:00\fP.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-disable\-signals
Disable signal handling (required for running under valgrind).
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-disable\-gc
Disable the garbage collector for deterministic collection.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-warnings\-are\-errors
Treat warnings as errors.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-enable\-all\-warnings
Enable all non-strict warnings (recommended).
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-warnings
Enable strict warnings (ambiguous overloads/calls).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-enable\-warning =\fIwarning\fP
Enable a specific warning by name.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-list\-warnings
List all available warning names and exit.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-list\-parse\-options
List all parse option names and exit.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-parse\-option\-help
Display descriptions of all parse options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-lgpl\fR, \fB\-\-mit
Set the library license flag to LGPL or MIT.
GPL-licensed modules cannot be loaded when this is set.
.SS "AOT Compilation Options"
.TP
.B \-\-compile
Compile a Qore program to a standalone executable instead of executing it.
.TP
.B \-\-output =\fIfile\fP
Set the output file for \fB\-\-compile\fP.
The default is the input file name with the extension stripped.
.TP
.B \-\-opt\-level =\fIN\fP
Set the AOT compiler optimization level from 0 to 3.
The default is 2 for \fBqore --compile\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-target =\fItriple\fP
Compile for the given LLVM target triple.
The default is the native host target.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-targets
Show supported target architectures and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-static
Statically link libqore into the generated executable.
This requires Qore to have been built with \fBBUILD_STATIC_LIBQORE=ON\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-compile\-module
Compile a \fB.qm\fP user module to a native shared-library binary module.
.PP
For full AOT workflows, including \fB.qo\fP relocatable objects,
\fB.qoa\fP archives, split-module compilation, dependency files, metadata
inspection, and source/debug stripping options, use \fBqcc\fP(1).
.SS "Module and Path Information"
.TP
.B \-\-module\-dir
Show the binary module directory and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-user\-module\-dir
Show the user module directory and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-module\-path
Show the full module search path and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-module\-api
Show the compatible module API version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-module\-apis
Show all supported module API versions and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-latest\-module\-api
Show the most recent module API version and exit.
.SS "Character Set Information"
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-show\-charsets
Display the list of known character set encodings.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-show\-aliases
Display the list of character set aliases.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-show\-build\-options
Show Qore build options and exit.
.SS "REPL Options"
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
Force interactive REPL mode even when stdin is not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-repl
Disable the automatic REPL when stdin is a terminal.
.SS "Parse Options"
These options restrict what constructs are legal in the parsed program,
enabling sandboxing.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-enable\-debug
Enable @debug and @assert statements.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-modern
Turn on recommended parse options.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-global\-vars
Make global variable definitions illegal.
.SS "Debugging Options"
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug =\fIlevel\fP
Set the internal debugging level (higher = more output).
Only available in debug builds.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-trace
Enable function call tracing.
Only available in debug builds.
.TP
.B \-\-only\-first\-exception
Stop after the first parsing exception instead of showing all.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QORE_MODULE_DIR
Colon-separated list of directories to search for Qore modules,
prepended to the default module path.
.TP
.B QORE_INCLUDE_DIR
Colon-separated list of directories to search for include files.
.TP
.B QORE_LIBDIR
Directory containing libqore, used by AOT-compiled programs and \fBqcc\fP
when resolving the runtime library.
.TP
.B QORE_CHARSET
Default character encoding if not specified with \fB\-c\fP.
.TP
.B TZ
Fallback time zone if not specified with \fB\-z\fP.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fBqore\fR returns 0 on success.
A non-zero exit status indicates an error occurred during parsing or execution,
or reflects the value passed to \fBexit()\fP by the program.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/qore
The \fBqore\fP interpreter (default installation path).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a script:
.RS
.B qore myprog.q
.RE
.PP
Evaluate an expression:
.RS
.B qore \-X '2 + 2'
.RE
.PP
Execute inline code:
.RS
.B qore \-e 'printf(\(dqhello world\en\(dq);'
.RE
.PP
Start an interactive REPL:
.RS
.B qore
.RE
.PP
Run only the AST interpreter:
.RS
.B qore --exec-mode=ast myprog.q
.RE
.PP
Run with explicit JIT compilation:
.RS
.B qore --exec-mode=jit myprog.q
.RE
.PP
Compile a script to a native executable:
.RS
.B qore --compile -o myprog myprog.qr
.RE
